Without holding `hdev` lock, another thread can free the `hci_conn` concurrently after the lookup, causing a use-after-free when accessing `conn->passkey_notify`. The early return also exits without any lock protection.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
+hci_dev_lock(hdev);
+conn = hci_conn_hash_lookup_ba(hdev, ACL_LINK, &ev->bdaddr);
+if (!conn)
+    goto unlock;
+...
+unlock:
